So, here we are gonna learn about Link List. Link list is a linear data structure. In link list, there are nodes
that are connected with the next node. Each of the nodes contain two parts, one is the data that it stores and 
the other is the memory address of the next node. And just like lists, you will have to access the elements
thru traversing. That is through O(n) time complexity.

And to traverse every node, you need a Head pointer(Head*) which points to the first element of the list and
a Tail pointer(Tail*) which points to the last element of the list. And just like list, link list also has
4 major functions. 
1. push_front--> inserts elements at the front of the list
2. push_back-->inserts elements at the back of the list
3. pop_front-->removes elements from the front of the list
4. pop_back-->removes elements from the back of the list


So, in lists, we have seen direct implementations of these and the initialization of the lists directly
but here, we will see it from the scratch. Mostly, we will use classes and objects to study link list here.
We will see them thru examples.

